nio: put the fork main-thread marks on printf

The panel reaches execve (LD pre-execve) and stops at "FC pre-main_thread"
with no following mark.  The FC marks use the direct framebuffer writer and
can be scrolled off the 40-line panel, so this round switches the two
main-thread marks to printf -- the writer proven to survive in kern_exec.c:

  nio: FX pre-main-thread          before main_thread_create_waiting
  nio: FX post-main-thread err=N   after it, with the return code

If pre shows without post, main_thread_create_waiting() is the blocking call;
the existing task_create marks (FC pre/post-task_create) stay as-is.
Diagnosis only: no behaviour change.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_fork.c b/bsd/kern/kern_fork.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_fork.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_fork.c
@@ -515,7 +515,7 @@
 	 *
 	 * The new thread is waiting on the event triggered by 'task_clear_return_wait'
 	 */
-	nio_fmark("\nnio: FC pre-main_thread");
+	printf("\nnio: FX pre-main-thread\n");
 	result = main_thread_create_waiting(child_task,
 	    (thread_continue_t)task_wait_to_return,
 	    task_get_return_wait_event(child_task),
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
 		child_task = NULL;
 	}
 
-	nio_fmark("\nnio: FC post-main_thread");
+	printf("\nnio: FX post-main-thread err=%d\n", result);
 
 	/*
 	 * Tag thread as being the first thread in its task.
